{% doc %}
  Outputs "hidden" when a product must not be listed in search, and nothing otherwise (D-092):
  1. a product priced at zero, which is not sold on its own (D-070);
  2. an IBO pack (product type Packs), unless the shopper is signed in as an IBO. Exigo customer types 2 and 3 are IBOs,
     the same test the Exigo storefront script uses; type 1 is a retail customer.
  The product's own address keeps working: the IBO collection and the enrolment links use it.

  @param {product} product - The product in the search results

  @example
  {% capture lp_hidden %}{% render 'lp-search-hidden', product: item %}{% endcapture %}
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  if product.price_max == 0 and product.gift_card? == false
    echo 'hidden'
  elsif product.type == 'Packs'
    assign exigo_type = customer.metafields.Exigo.CustomerTypeId.value | default: customer.metafields.Exigo.CustomerTypeId | append: '' | strip
    unless exigo_type == '2' or exigo_type == '3'
      echo 'hidden'
    endunless
  endif
-%}
